<Project>

  <!--
    Documentation is a compiler-checked property of this tree, not a review
    convention. GenerateDocumentationFile turns on CS1591 (a publicly visible
    type or member with no XML comment) and CS1573 (a parameter with no
    matching param tag), so "every public member is documented, and every
    parameter is covered" becomes a build result rather than something someone
    has to re-audit by reading.

    Scoped to src/ deliberately. Tests live under tests/ and are exempt: a
    [Fact] named NobodyRetreatsFromASettledBlob already is the sentence a
    summary would restate, and the same holds for the benchmark harness.

    Where a member really is self-describing, suppress CS1591 with a narrow
    pragma at the declaration and say why. A blanket NoWarn here would turn the
    whole question back into an unenforced convention, which is the state this
    file exists to leave.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
